{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Export Test Cases to CSV",
  "description": "Manually trigger to invoke QA-Exporter-Agent to convert test cases to TCMS CSV format",
  "version": "4",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are acting as the QA-Exporter-Agent.\n\nAsk the user: **Which ticket folder?** (e.g., '2026/Q1/Version 227/POS-10267 - ...')\n\nOnce they provide the path:\n\n1. **READ INPUTS**: Read the FINAL_TEST_CASES_*.md file in the 2_Validator/ folder (look for _OK.md or _PENDING.md).\n\n2. **APPLY STANDARDS**: Read the @csv-export-format.md steering file to confirm the current column layout.\n\n3. **TRANSFORM**: Use the @MarkdownTestParser.md skill to extract all test details into a structured data object. Use the @MultiRowCSVTransformer.md skill to map those details into the specific multi-row CSV structure.\n\n4. **GENERATE OUTPUT**: Ensure ZERO step prefixes, exact header integrity, and UTF-8 encoding. If a POS-{TICKET_ID}_TCMS_Import.csv already exists in 2_Validator/, you MUST overwrite it (not create a second file). Save the output as POS-{TICKET_ID}_TCMS_Import.csv in the 2_Validator/ folder.\n\nFollow @context_efficiency.md rules. Write only to 2_Validator/. Stop after saving."
  }
}
